WEBVTT

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.620
Angelo, Stan Fabian.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.760
Yeah, look, I want 50 across on Lady Gentry in the third,

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.270
and I want $100 to show on Speedy Kid in the fifth.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:26.350
Okay, I'll call you later.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:26.730
Right.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.270
I only got two hands, you know.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.150
Well, shake it up.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.340
Some horn-happy creep just pulled in.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:47.690
Let him honk.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.040
If it isn't long-shot stand,

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.830
how come you're not at the track on a nice, quiet day like this,

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:54.100
playing a favorite?

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.380
Why should I be? I got a sure thing right here.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:06.600
Hi, Joanie.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:07.720
What are you doing here?

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:08.920
On my way to Chicago.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:09.920
Pick up a stack.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.510
Well, don't let me keep you.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:12.460
Hey, wait a minute.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.180
I'm thirsty.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.630
Dan, hand me the waffles, will you?

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:16.230
Sure.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.030
Something I can do for you?

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.270
I just dropped in to see my sister.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:34.210
She'll work here?

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:35.760
Yeah, Joan Daniel.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:37.830
You're not Frank, are you?

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:38.350
That's right.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.560
Why don't you say so? I'm Stan Fabian.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.120
Well, glad to know you.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:42.820
I'm glad to know you, too.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:44.540
Heard all about you.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:45.840
Oh, from Joanie?

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.610
Yeah. She told us she was working for a very nice guy.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.150
Order, Stan.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.860
Okay. Some surprise, huh, honey?

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.720
Yeah, Frank is full of surprises.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.320
Always kidding, now, kid.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:02:59.860
Where'd you get in town?

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.980
Just now, I feel like I'm still riding.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:03.100
Like something to drink?

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.230
Okay, root beer'd be fine.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:08.260
Right. How about something to eat?

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.260
I had lunch in Santa Barbara.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.960
Tell me, how are all the folks up in Portland?

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.560
Okay, sounds like Joni told you all about us.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.020
Ah, just give him the whole rundown.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:21.010
128 out of 5.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:24.670
Here you are, honey.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.780
You're not staying a while?

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:29.900
No, I'm going on to Chicago.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.480
That is if if is right if you think I'm gonna give you any money for this crazy deal of yours

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:40.840
You're wasting your time you talk too much big mouth what the it's all right Stan

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.750
I just want him to know how things stand well, just don't pop off in front of strangers. It's none of their business

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:49.440
I'm not exactly a stranger Joni and I are pretty good friends

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:57.150
That's nice work if you can get it and it looks like you are you don't you think you're getting a little out of line?

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.480
So I'm sorry. I shouldn't have said it

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.700
Why don't you give that mind of yours an airing?

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:02.990
Ah, that's all right, honey.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.940
I guess a brother's got a right to worry about his sister.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.980
Who cares? I can take care of myself.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.960
What do you say we all have dinner down at the barn tonight, okay?

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:13.460
No, I don't want to barge in.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.460
You're not barging in. Be my guest.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.200
Ah, come on, honey. You know the slogan of this place.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.140
Service with a smile.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.860
Let me see a smile on that pretty little kissery.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.530
Ha-ha. Atta girl.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.180
Just a natural-born umpire.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.760
Come on, Frank. We'll get you cleaned up.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.560
So by the time that I got out of the army, I was a pretty good cook.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.550
I had a couple of thousand dollars saved up, and I put it in the beehive.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.600
Kind of tough at first, doing all the cooking.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:52.610
Listen, Stan, can't we talk about something else besides his ride in?

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.940
Get enough of that place wrassling trays all day.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.820
You wouldn't have to wrassle trays if you'd listen to reason.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.800
I mean, the kind of reason that goes on the third finger in the left hand.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.460
You sound like a bad proposition to me, Joanie.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.960
Not if I don't mind placing second to a horse.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.040
Made long shots, Dan.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.210
On top of the world today and a hock tomorrow.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:17.850
No, sir.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.370
When I get married, I want to have some security.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.540
I want a home and a family.

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.960
The only ponies I want to hear about are the Shetlands for the kids.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.120
I'll quit tomorrow. I'll put it in writing.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:29.980
Well, where?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.600
on the back of a scratch sheet?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.220
Joni, better take it a little easy.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.720
Who sent for you?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:42.200
Come on, honey. Frank, tell me,

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.170
his deal in Chicago takes a little capital?

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.080
Oh, yeah.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:48.020
How much?

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:48.880
$3,000.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:50.570
Give me a bag of shelves.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.300
$3,000, huh?

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.120
Well, don't look at me.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.580
If you want to loan him the money, it's your funeral.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:58.930
Just don't blame me.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.540
Tell him what it's about. The big goose chase.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:06.040
All right, all right. There you go, spouting off again.

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.140
Some umpire, huh?

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:13.100
Oh, I'm sorry, Stan. I'm sorry I loused up your evening.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.750
You couldn't louse up our evening, could he, honey?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.210
Like to finish this dance?

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.550
That's the best idea I've ever heard tonight.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:18.800
I saw her hit her all of a sudden.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:23.030
Well, that's a Daniel for you. Baseball drinkers. Three drinks and they're out.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:29.000
I think I better take her home.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:34.060
I'll say you're gonna go to the Rainbow Room.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:38.790
Okay.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.310
I'll wait here. See you tomorrow, Julie.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.220
Who cares? Come on, Stan.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.280
Let's go to the Rainbow Room.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:07:59.620
Okay, sweetheart. We'll go to the Rainbow Room.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:14.340
Come on. I guess you can tell I'm pretty nuts about that kid, huh?

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.640
Well, all I can say is keep punching, pal.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.270
Punching? I've been knocking myself out.

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:25.030
I got a rule, you know, never fool around with any of the carhops.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:28.880
It's a business. And along comes Joanie and out goes the rule.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:36.100
Oh, boy, she's a real doll. All she ever wanted was work, nothing else.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.420
She's all work and no play, always has been that kid.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.790
She's out for one thing, security.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:48.220
Security. Some girls, that's a mink coat and a million dollars,

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.930
and with others, it's three squares a day and a roof over your head. You figure it.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.120
You only tell me about your deal. What deal?

00:08:59.260 --> 00:08:59.960
All right, don't get so.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:06.140
Maybe she was loaded. Maybe she was making the whole thing up.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:13.780
Yeah, maybe she was. What did she tell you?

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:15.830
Oh, I don't know. It was something about, uh,

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:19.560
some gold knickknacks that you liberated from some chateau

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:20.320
while you were in the army.

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.610
Rather, what a few drinks will do.

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:25.730
Now, worth about, uh, $200,000.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.000
What else did she tell you?

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:29.970
Oh, that you had a...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.600
I had a partner, a buddy in Chicago that you were meeting on the 1st.

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:36.910
That's why you needed the dough,

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:41.880
because you and his partner were supposed to each put up $3,000 to finance the trip.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:44.340
Well, that Joni should be a writer.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:46.840
What's still there?

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:48.880
I don't know anything.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.670
Suppose I'm willing to invest $3,000 to find out.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:54.540
Look, save your dough. That won't help you any with Joni.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.130
We'll wind up marrying you, all right.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:09:59.980
May not show it, but she likes s***.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:08.380
she's not the only reason that i'm interested 200 000 bucks is a lot of scratch even half of it

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:26.940
isn't bad the deal is between the other guy and me just the two of us so forget it huh sleep on it

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:29.040
will you frank i'll see you in the morning night

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:42.340
Who is it?

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:43.950
Joanie?

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:47.070
Don.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:57.200
Who's it, Ben?

00:10:58.530 --> 00:10:58.890
Billionaire.

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:02.850
Thank heaven you're here.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:20.460
Mighty cute drunk.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:22.590
That was practically no act.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:25.100
How are we doing?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.530
We've got him hooked.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.860
I hope so. I don't know how much longer I can hold him off.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:37.630
Yeah, he certainly took his time, uh, saying goodnight to you tonight.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:41.890
He takes his free time every night. That's the trouble.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:44.280
You just keep sparring, Monty.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:47.260
He may be bigger than you are, but you've got the speed.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.180
Thought I'd step by and let you know how things were going.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.460
A little behind.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.280
Thought any more about what we were talking about last night?

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:06.980
Yeah, I have.

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.140
You looked at a calendar lately?

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.800
Haven't got much time left, have you?

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:17.510
What's with Johnny this morning?

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:18.830
It's half past nine already.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:19.830
Oh, she'll be here.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:23.710
Good old lad.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:25.890
He's the best short-order man there is.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:27.510
I had to give him a piece of the joint to keep him.

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:27.850
Yeah?

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:29.630
I'm sorry, I'm late, Stan.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:29.970
Oh, that's...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.160
That's all right, honey. How do you feel?

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.500
Like my head stuck on with scotch tape.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:35.560
How do you take the day off?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.580
I'll be all right after I have a cup of tea.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:46.880
Sure, okay. She works real hard, that kid.

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:48.530
Always has, all her life.

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:50.790
Maybe she deserves a break.

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:56.740
Stan, how would you like to take Joanie to Europe on your honeymoon?

00:12:58.850 --> 00:12:59.470
Are you kidding?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.770
No, she's always dreamed about traveling and seeing the world.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:08.430
She used to flip every time I'd tell her about some of the places I'd seen overseas.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:15.750
Well, I think she might go for the European trip, but the honeymoon, I don't know.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.930
You can sell her once she knows you're in on the deal.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:21.320
What about your partner?

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:25.770
If he won't cut you in, I'll split my half with you.

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:28.790
Tell you what I'll do.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:34.890
If Joanie goes for it, you got a deal, but you got to sell it.

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:44.240
Well, if it ain't the queen bee, what brings you to the hive this morning?

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:47.500
It's a great day for making honey, honey.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.990
Well, here I am. Where is everybody?

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:52.950
Oh, they'll be back.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.820
Maybe I'd have to take off the slacks and put on a bikini bathing suit.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.240
Yeah, if you did that, honey, we'd have to beat them off with a stick.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:13:59.970
Joanie, honey.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.720
How would you like to take a little trip to Europe?

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:02.560
With you?

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:03.770
And Stan.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:06.900
I told you Frankie was full of surprises.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.860
What's the angle this time?

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:10.530
Stan's in on the deal.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.670
You just can't resist a long shot, can you?

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.110
Honey, I haven't said yes yet.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:18.980
Go ahead, Frankie. Tell us all about it.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.880
Well, you and Stan could make it a honeymoon.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.880
A honeymoon? Me and Stan?

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.760
Listen, Cupid, what makes you think I'm ready for a honeymoon?

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.440
You're always talking about security.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.200
100,000 bucks is a lot of security.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.320
How do you feel about it, Stan?

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:38.890
You know the way I feel about you.

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.900
You just say the word and we go.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:43.580
I'll tell you what.

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:46.390
Suppose we start the honeymoon after we have the money.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.380
Miss Daniel, turn in your uniform.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:49.670
But what about the place?

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:50.410
Who's going to run it?

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:52.970
Ed can run it with his brother Randy in a couple of carhops.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:54.780
It's a little more.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:14:59.160
What do you say, honey?

00:14:59.240 --> 00:14:59.980
Shall I go down and get us?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:08.600
passport i don't know you're coming at me awful fast what do you say honey oh dad

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.670
Here you come, sweetheart. Come on, wake up.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.160
You gotta make a good impression on your brother's buddy, okay?

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:49.030
Ray, kid sister Joni and her husband-to-be, Stan Fabian, Ray Torres.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.240
I don't, uh, get this.

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:53.380
Well, I'll explain everything. Come on, get in.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:56.250
I think we ought to have a little talk first.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.960
Oh, we'll talk on the way. Come on, let's go.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:08.770
Where to?

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:09.710
Tell him, Rick.

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:12.200
Right ahead to the outer drive.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.670
So Stan here offered to put up my end of the dough

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:20.720
and make it a honeymoon for him and Joanie.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:22.760
That wasn't our deal. You know that.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:26.140
Yeah, but I figured, you know, something should come up,

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.800
that we needed more dough. Stan could put it up for both of us.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:29.980
It's worth it just for the...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:36.040
insurance i don't need insurance so i'll cut him in for half of mine you ain't cutting him in on

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:40.360
nothing where do you get off telling him about this in the first place this was a two-way deal

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:45.220
just between you and me you've got a lot of guts trying to cut your family in wait a minute if i'm

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:49.380
willing to split my half with stan that's no skin off you it's going to be the way we set it up

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:59.560
or nothing i mean or nothing i go single oh that isn't very practical the circumstances

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.820
What circumstances?

00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:04.220
Well, you see, there are several of us that know about this now.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.880
Yeah, I can take care of that, too.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.800
All right, chum, take me back to the hotel.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:10.990
What was that?

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:11.930
My silencer.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:12.610
Keep driving!

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:13.410
Are you nuts?

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.140
All right, pull over to the side!

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.440
Slow down!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:29.900
Slow down, do you want a cop on her?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.230
I didn't figure on anything like this.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:36.630
You killed him. You killed him!

00:17:36.830 --> 00:17:39.580
Put yourself together. Don't give me any choice.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:04.560
Where are we? Ohio someplace.

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.340
Looks like a town up there ahead. Why don't we stop?

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.400
Joni's all knocked out.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.690
The further we get from Chicago, the better.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.160
Here's an early morning bullet.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:17.340
Body of Ramon Torres, Chicago-used car salesman,

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:20.690
was found floating in Lake Michigan outside of Chicago early this morning.

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:24.510
Police are looking for two men and a girl in a light-colored convertible,

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.370
which is believed to be the killer's car.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:29.260
Police ruled out robbery as the motive of the crime.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.140
He discovered $3,200 in the victim's wallet.

00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.940
Lionel Boyd, clerk of the Monarch Hotel.

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:36.900
What are we gonna do?

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:37.720
Just take it easy.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:40.800
They haven't got the make of the car.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.560
I don't like that two-man-and-a-girl business.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.120
We ought to split up.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.200
Yeah, you take a plane to New York.

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:48.200
Joni and I will meet you there.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:49.260
Good idea.

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:50.370
What do we do it the other way?

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:51.190
You take the plane.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.170
Joni goes with me.

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:53.760
I wanna go with Stan.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:54.860
We do it my way.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:56.460
If we're picked up, we're brother and sister.

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:56.880
Legit.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.620
I wanna go home.

00:18:58.920 --> 00:18:59.960
Nobody's going back home.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.000
and we're all in this together.

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:04.330
These suckers not to go through with it now.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:06.320
Over 100,000 apiece.

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:08.200
Frank, he's right.

00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:09.760
Honey, we'd be suckers to quit now.

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:11.470
Everything's gonna be all right.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:15.240
There's a gas station. Why'd you pull up?

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:25.980
I'll take a cab to the airport.

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:36.020
Here, bring the rest of the stuff with us.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:39.720
Give me some dough for expenses.

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:43.920
When you get to New York, check in to the Caxton Hotel and wait for us.

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.990
We'll get there as fast as we can. It's 200.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:55.200
Do it. Remember, the Caxton Hotel on West 39th Street.

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:56.400
Bye, Dad.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:57.740
Please wait for us, Dad.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:08.900
Take it easy, darling. Don't overdo it.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:10.610
That was quite a shock to Stan.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.730
Wait till he gets the big shock.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:27.070
Boat tickets, bill from the Monaco Hotel, paid in full.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:29.040
Passport.

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:34.730
And 3,200 smack-a-roos.

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:38.920
Sure ain't to part with all that scratch, Mr. Jackson.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.130
It felt kind of good just carrying it around, you know?

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:43.780
Well, you keep it then, Ray.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.660
Mr. Atherton would want you to for doing such a good job.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.990
Oh, well, thank him for me. That's wonderful.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.730
You can send them in now, Miss Swanson.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.500
Before you go, there's a good friend of yours here who would like to say hello.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:20:58.900
Frank!

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:00.890
Ray, how do you feel?

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.250
Well, if you'd waited till we got a few yards down the road,

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:04.590
I wouldn't have had to take that bath.

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:05.930
I couldn't see the water.

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:06.730
Oh, sure.

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.230
Anyway, it was Saturday night.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.590
At these prices, I'd get waterlogged.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.230
Don't forget now, for the time being,

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:13.930
stay out of New York and Frankfurt, Germany.

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:15.530
Don't worry about it.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:16.690
I'm going to Vegas.

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:20.920
By the way, how'd our shortwave broadcast come through?

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.150
Oh, he got the message.

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:23.870
He couldn't wait to take off for New York.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:25.990
So far, everything's going right on schedule.

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:27.580
Well, let's hope it continues.

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:29.970
We're close to the end now, and Mr. Atherton is getting...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.280
very anxious how about you miss morrow everything all right now that frank's into it i feel much

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:42.310
safer this past year hasn't been too easy i can imagine yeah without her we never would have

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:47.980
made it she's got him to a point now where he'll do almost anything she asks him to that remains to

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:57.130
be seen frank yes we're ready now mr otherton fine bring him in mr derling will be along any

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:59.830
A moment now, gentlemen. I'll have him fill you in on the background.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:02.490
Dirling's been on in this case for a long time.

00:22:03.080 --> 00:22:04.500
He knows every aspect of it.

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.050
Joanie, wonderful.

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:10.850
Frank.

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:12.270
R.B., good to see you again.

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:13.830
Frank, you know the boys.

00:22:14.130 --> 00:22:14.610
Hi, boys.

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:17.600
This is Herr Koenig, Frank.

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:19.020
Just arrived from Berlin.

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:20.090
Herr Koenig?

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:21.530
Sayang an him.

00:22:22.540 --> 00:22:24.380
Miss Morrow and my attorney, Tom Jackson.

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:26.620
Herr Koenig of the German police.

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:29.400
Now, I want you to tell them the story.

00:22:30.030 --> 00:22:32.560
Mr. Derling, here, gentlemen, was an eyewitness.

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:34.550
The whole picture, sir?

00:22:34.750 --> 00:22:35.650
From beginning to end.

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:39.300
I want all of you men to have every single detail on this case.

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:43.590
If the boys here know what we're working for, it'll help them do a better job.

00:22:44.040 --> 00:22:44.300
Yes, sir.

00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:49.820
Well, gentlemen, our story goes back to November 6th, 1945,

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:51.680
after the occupation of Berlin.

00:22:52.820 --> 00:22:54.720
The division quartermaster received a tip

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:57.180
that there was a quantity of stolen supplies

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:59.520
in a bombed-out bakery near Neustadt.

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:05.250
He notified battalion headquarters, and they sent an MP lieutenant,

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:10.140
Mr. Atherton's son, with a detail of us to investigate.

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:16.920
It looked like anything was alive in the whole town.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:23.820
Please!

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:29.460
Get everything you can hold on to and go out the back way.

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:29.920
I'll keep moving.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:45.100
I told you, we'll never make it, we'll never make it!

00:23:58.900 --> 00:23:59.260
You're good.

00:24:03.160 --> 00:24:03.880
Why'd you never make it?

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:11.840
You'll never make it.

00:24:12.440 --> 00:24:13.280
Get out of here!

00:24:28.310 --> 00:24:29.980
This was a one-man op-

00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:36.110
Colonel Riegel had been assigned to the case.

00:24:36.780 --> 00:24:39.720
He established that the bullet had been fired from an M1 rifle,

00:24:40.170 --> 00:24:43.430
but more important, when Riegel discovered powder burns around the wound,

00:24:44.070 --> 00:24:48.210
he concluded that the dead GI had been shot from behind and at close range.

00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:50.520
A thorough investigation was ordered.

00:24:51.700 --> 00:24:54.960
Several arrests were made, but all suspects were finally released.

00:24:55.780 --> 00:24:59.980
Apparently, up a blind alley, a new strategy was decided upon to uncover the...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:05.900
killer the man they called pack rat all weapons in the outfit were ordered to be turned in for

00:25:05.900 --> 00:25:11.540
survey and new ones issued then each of these weapons were fired into a ballistics recovery box

00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:16.850
each bullet was carefully retrieved from the cotton and tagged with the number of the weapon

00:25:16.850 --> 00:25:22.710
that had fired the slugs were flown to the states for ballistics tests it was a long

00:25:22.710 --> 00:25:24.070
painstaking operation.

00:25:25.380 --> 00:25:29.970
I hope to find the bullet of Killer Pat.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:38.600
among the first tests finally after two weeks operation haystack was over rifle number m126891

00:25:38.600 --> 00:25:47.180
was issued to fabian stanley e sergeant cook 189 4th battalion they were all set to lower the boom

00:25:47.180 --> 00:25:52.440
when they got a bad break back red stan had been returned to the states and honorably discharged

00:25:52.440 --> 00:25:59.050
the army was powerless to prosecute him for his crime that's the story gentlemen

00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:02.660
we've been planning and waiting for the right moment to move.

00:26:03.050 --> 00:26:03.650
Now it's here.

00:26:04.240 --> 00:26:08.160
Last year, Miss Morrow succeeded in getting a job working for this Fabian fellow.

00:26:08.590 --> 00:26:10.110
She has his complete confidence.

00:26:10.590 --> 00:26:13.750
Now Frank, who has been planning everything, has moved in.

00:26:14.230 --> 00:26:15.330
The rest is up to you.

00:26:15.650 --> 00:26:19.170
Each one of you will be thoroughly briefed on the part that you're going to play.

00:26:19.980 --> 00:26:20.940
Any questions, gentlemen?

00:26:21.230 --> 00:26:23.180
Herr Koenig, you got any problems?

00:26:23.380 --> 00:26:25.200
Problem? No problem.

00:26:25.840 --> 00:26:29.970
All you got to do is bring this fellow Fabian to Germany and give us the...

00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:33.560
The deutsche Polizei will do the rest.

00:26:34.340 --> 00:26:35.160
No problems.

00:26:35.860 --> 00:26:37.780
All right, then. Let's get to work.

00:26:38.460 --> 00:26:40.040
Mr. Jackson. This way, gentlemen.

00:26:40.580 --> 00:26:41.760
And good luck to you all.

00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:48.910
Joni, you've done a remarkable job.

00:26:49.390 --> 00:26:51.500
Won't be long now. You too, Frank.

00:26:52.180 --> 00:26:53.540
And you know, after this is over with,

00:26:53.740 --> 00:26:56.060
I have some plans for you, too,

00:26:56.320 --> 00:26:57.540
that I think you're going to like.

00:26:58.620 --> 00:26:59.900
We have a few plans of our own.

00:27:00.030 --> 00:27:03.230
Well, that's fine, but don't forget, the honeymoon's on me.

00:27:04.090 --> 00:27:09.190
Frank, I've arranged to take over the von Reimer estate in Frankfort on the 18th of this month.

00:27:09.570 --> 00:27:10.770
We'll have a 90-day lease.

00:27:11.160 --> 00:27:11.880
Oh, that'll be plenty.

00:27:12.080 --> 00:27:14.840
I've also arranged with my bank for you to have unlimited funds.

00:27:15.080 --> 00:27:16.720
Anything you need will be at your disposal.

00:27:17.170 --> 00:27:17.930
Well, thank you.

00:27:21.720 --> 00:27:22.500
That's it, I guess.

00:27:31.500 --> 00:27:37.830
But you know, after we've finished with this, it still won't bring back my son to me, will it?

00:27:39.100 --> 00:27:40.280
He meant a great deal to me.

00:27:41.340 --> 00:27:46.360
All this, everything I own, everything I possess, was for my son.

00:27:56.180 --> 00:27:57.000
Godspeed both of them.

00:27:58.620 --> 00:27:59.360
Do our best, Herbie.

00:28:30.220 --> 00:28:35.200
Joni, how'd you get here so fast?

00:28:35.460 --> 00:28:37.140
We left the car in Akron and took a plane.

00:28:37.480 --> 00:28:37.880
You did what?

00:28:38.380 --> 00:28:40.300
We got stopped in Toledo and again in Cleveland.

00:28:41.010 --> 00:28:42.670
I figured the crate was getting too hot.

00:28:43.620 --> 00:28:46.300
I was sure the cop could hear my heart pounding. I was so scared.

00:28:46.760 --> 00:28:47.940
Never should have let you out of my sight.

00:28:47.940 --> 00:28:50.560
I'm all right now, and look how much sooner we're together.

00:28:51.690 --> 00:28:53.030
It's the best reason for my money.

00:28:55.380 --> 00:28:56.720
Come on, come on, let's get squared away.

00:28:57.040 --> 00:28:58.300
You've got plenty of time for that.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:00.940
Oh, Frank, relax.

00:29:02.040 --> 00:29:03.800
There's a freighter leaving Thursday for England.

00:29:04.240 --> 00:29:04.940
We can get on it.

00:29:05.300 --> 00:29:05.920
A freighter?

00:29:06.720 --> 00:29:09.820
I thought we were going on something like the Queen Mary or the Ile de France.

00:29:10.120 --> 00:29:11.680
Oh, honey, I don't like it too much either,

00:29:11.800 --> 00:29:14.360
but you just wait until we get our hands on that big dough.

00:29:15.120 --> 00:29:18.990
I promise you we'll come back on the biggest tub of floatin'.

00:29:19.360 --> 00:29:20.360
And first class.

00:29:36.780 --> 00:29:38.120
Not bad for a freighter, huh?

00:29:38.880 --> 00:29:41.120
Yeah, I had pictured freight all over the place.

00:29:42.130 --> 00:29:44.490
And I pictured myself rooming with a tractor or something.

00:29:46.040 --> 00:29:48.200
I never knew an ocean voyage could be so relaxing.

00:29:48.790 --> 00:29:50.330
Why, Slim Durling!

00:29:50.510 --> 00:29:55.210
Who got me mixed up with somebody else?

00:29:55.870 --> 00:29:57.310
Always the clown, huh?

00:29:57.550 --> 00:29:59.670
Say, who do you think's beating me over in England?

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:02.020
Doc Mason and Charlie Holt.

00:30:02.280 --> 00:30:03.920
Boy, what a small boat.

00:30:04.340 --> 00:30:06.540
Look, fella, you've got me mixed up with somebody.

00:30:06.840 --> 00:30:08.960
Oh, come off the rim, Slim Dooling.

00:30:09.060 --> 00:30:11.980
I'd know that face of yours if I saw it in a bear cave.

00:30:12.200 --> 00:30:13.980
Well, maybe so, but I don't know yours.

00:30:14.620 --> 00:30:15.920
What's the matter with you, Slim?

00:30:16.920 --> 00:30:19.360
We spent two years together in the same outfit.

00:30:19.960 --> 00:30:21.320
Angelo Salerno.

00:30:21.960 --> 00:30:25.720
Hey, remember Maria? Salerno, huh?

00:30:26.050 --> 00:30:29.230
Look, fella, I'm Frank Daniel, and you're becoming a pest.

00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:33.110
Well, if, uh, if you're not Slim Dirling, uh...

00:30:33.110 --> 00:30:33.970
I'll take one of those.

00:30:38.360 --> 00:30:41.130
Oh, uh, a wife, huh?

00:30:42.220 --> 00:30:43.640
This happens to be my sister.

00:30:44.940 --> 00:30:46.460
And if you ever run into that friend of yours,

00:30:46.720 --> 00:30:48.760
tell him I'm sorry for him if he looks like Frank.

00:30:48.960 --> 00:30:54.460
I guess I could be wrong, but, uh,

00:30:55.690 --> 00:30:57.750
never saw anything like it.

00:30:57.890 --> 00:30:59.980
This happens to me all...

00:31:00.420 --> 00:31:03.260
I've been taken for everybody from Cary Grant to Gandy.

00:31:03.480 --> 00:31:05.080
You should only look like Cary Grant.

00:31:06.220 --> 00:31:07.880
And I don't see why you got so annoyed.

00:31:08.100 --> 00:31:09.500
You practically insulted the man.

00:31:09.960 --> 00:31:10.800
What am I supposed to do?

00:31:10.980 --> 00:31:12.640
Stand here and start yakking with the guy?

00:31:13.380 --> 00:31:15.260
This is no time to start conversation.

00:31:17.430 --> 00:31:18.350
I'm about to turn around the deck.

00:31:19.030 --> 00:31:20.310
I want to stay here and get some sun.

00:31:20.940 --> 00:31:21.200
Stan?

00:31:21.980 --> 00:31:23.500
I want to stay right here.

00:31:24.630 --> 00:31:25.030
See you later.

00:31:28.660 --> 00:31:29.480
You better stay there.

00:31:32.970 --> 00:31:35.910
Shoot your horns, Dan. I could use some curb service.

00:31:37.420 --> 00:31:39.440
Good idea, baby. I want to see him wait on you.

00:32:03.390 --> 00:32:03.790
Where is he?

00:32:05.060 --> 00:32:06.600
He's in some Penny Annie poker game.

00:32:09.050 --> 00:32:09.750
Hey, Slim!

00:32:10.860 --> 00:32:13.300
Slim, look, don't you remember, Maria?

00:32:13.720 --> 00:32:14.460
Shall I know?

00:32:14.820 --> 00:32:16.480
Stay away from me, will you?

00:32:20.480 --> 00:32:29.440
I hate to do that, too.

00:32:31.100 --> 00:32:34.260
Every time he sees me, he makes a beeline for the bar again.

00:32:36.200 --> 00:32:40.580
Hey, Slim, what about Maria? What about Salerno?

00:32:41.230 --> 00:32:42.390
That was another case.

00:32:42.840 --> 00:32:43.680
A case of what?

00:32:44.630 --> 00:32:45.350
Battle fatigue.

00:32:46.490 --> 00:32:46.950
You got it.

00:32:47.090 --> 00:32:53.370
Leave me alone.

00:32:53.670 --> 00:32:55.610
I got a right to talk to anybody I want to, see?

00:32:56.140 --> 00:32:59.220
I always said you talk too much the next time you open your yap, I'll...

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:04.080
Keep your hands off her.

00:33:04.700 --> 00:33:06.180
Jam us up with that mouth of hers.

00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:10.080
Coming out of the bar and here she is yacking with some old dame.

00:33:10.200 --> 00:33:12.980
Telling her we're going to Frankfurt, Germany to pick up an inheritance.

00:33:13.800 --> 00:33:15.620
Naming places, putting on the dog.

00:33:16.180 --> 00:33:17.960
You just keep your hands off her, you understand?

00:33:19.380 --> 00:33:21.540
Honey, you gotta be careful about talking to people, huh?

00:33:22.280 --> 00:33:23.240
Ma, I'll take it down to your cabin.

00:33:23.530 --> 00:33:25.720
I'll be all right. Why don't you go back to your game?

00:33:25.960 --> 00:33:27.260
Oh, that game is all over.

00:33:27.570 --> 00:33:29.970
I didn't want to play anymore, so we cut high card for the whole...

00:33:30.700 --> 00:33:31.260
60 cents.

00:33:38.660 --> 00:33:39.920
Take care of your jaw, Frankie.

00:33:40.180 --> 00:33:40.460
Yeah.

00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:01.520
Hey, there he is.

00:34:01.860 --> 00:34:02.520
Oh, God.

00:34:03.020 --> 00:34:05.500
Hey, Don! Down here! Come on!

00:34:05.820 --> 00:34:06.520
All right, boy.

00:34:06.960 --> 00:34:07.620
Fire door.

00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:11.560
What's keeping her?

00:34:12.650 --> 00:34:13.910
Take it easy. Take it easy.

00:34:14.010 --> 00:34:15.750
You know girls and their makeup and stuff.

00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:20.280
How are you? Good to see you.

00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:21.900
What happened to your hair?

00:34:22.080 --> 00:34:23.240
Never mind. No cracks, huh?

00:34:23.640 --> 00:34:24.800
I mean, boy, you got fat.

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:26.020
Well, what are you gonna do, you know?

00:34:26.350 --> 00:34:27.050
Let's go, huh?

00:34:27.170 --> 00:34:28.970
Now, wait a minute. Wait a minute.

00:34:29.400 --> 00:34:29.980
I want you to...

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.400
you fellas to see who's on this boat.

00:34:31.620 --> 00:34:32.440
Someone we know?

00:34:32.560 --> 00:34:33.600
Someone we know.

00:34:33.820 --> 00:34:34.900
Slim Durling.

00:34:35.020 --> 00:34:35.620
You're kidding.

00:34:36.080 --> 00:34:37.500
It's a doggone-est thing I ever saw.

00:34:37.600 --> 00:34:38.920
He insists he isn't Slim.

00:34:39.360 --> 00:34:40.820
I'll tell you, the guy drove me crazy.

00:34:41.020 --> 00:34:42.340
Maybe he just looks like Slim.

00:34:42.830 --> 00:34:43.990
Oh, no, it is Slim.

00:34:44.410 --> 00:34:46.330
He's traveling with his sister and her boyfriend.

00:34:46.610 --> 00:34:47.670
He doesn't have a sister.

00:34:47.790 --> 00:34:50.190
I spent a weekend with his family just before we went overseas.

00:34:50.510 --> 00:34:51.310
Okay, okay, okay.

00:34:51.470 --> 00:34:54.310
We'll wait till he gets off, and then you tell me if it's Slim or not.

00:34:56.690 --> 00:34:58.430
Why do we have to be the last ones off?

00:34:59.240 --> 00:34:59.880
She'll be here.

00:35:03.290 --> 00:35:04.910
Where is he? He'll be down in a minute.

00:35:05.430 --> 00:35:07.630
Not me. Don Gillan?

00:35:08.070 --> 00:35:09.770
Yeah, I'm Gillan. Scotland Yard.

00:35:09.950 --> 00:35:11.130
Scotland Yard, what is it?

00:35:11.290 --> 00:35:12.990
You'll come to me to the customs office, please.

00:35:13.620 --> 00:35:16.260
Costumes? What office is what's the question, sir?

00:35:17.870 --> 00:35:19.350
Can you gentlemen identify, Mr. Gillan?

00:35:19.510 --> 00:35:22.110
Oh, sure we can. Well, this is a fine, how do you do?

00:35:22.270 --> 00:35:24.710
Oh, don't worry about it, Don. We'll find out what this is all about.

00:35:24.990 --> 00:35:29.780
I left my robe out and I had to repack everything.

00:35:30.540 --> 00:35:31.440
Well, let's go, shall we?

00:35:57.440 --> 00:35:59.320
Will you have the bags taken up as soon as they come in, please?

00:36:02.840 --> 00:36:03.400
What's the next move?

00:36:03.580 --> 00:36:05.620
The first thing we ought to do is buy a car.

00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:07.060
What do you mean, buy a car?

00:36:07.310 --> 00:36:08.630
You're getting pretty sporty with my dough.

00:36:08.770 --> 00:36:09.550
What's the matter with the rented one?

00:36:10.270 --> 00:36:11.810
Rent one? We can buy one so cheap.

00:36:11.930 --> 00:36:12.870
Besides, we're going to need it.

00:36:13.170 --> 00:36:13.830
Come on, I'll show you.

00:36:13.990 --> 00:36:14.670
Wait a minute.

00:36:15.580 --> 00:36:16.840
Are we going upstairs for us?

00:36:17.160 --> 00:36:18.280
I'd like to freshen up.

00:36:18.440 --> 00:36:19.560
We can freshen up later.

00:36:19.700 --> 00:36:21.040
There's a car lot right down the street.

00:36:21.160 --> 00:36:22.580
They have all kinds of them cheap.

00:36:22.820 --> 00:36:23.060
Come on.

00:36:23.800 --> 00:36:26.320
Aren't you even going to send a cable to Ed and let him know where you're staying?

00:36:26.560 --> 00:36:27.220
Sure, sure.

00:36:27.340 --> 00:36:29.360
Just as soon as we see the sights.

00:36:39.120 --> 00:36:40.680
by the time I drove over this old road.

00:36:41.750 --> 00:36:44.150
Can you speed it up a little? You got the whole highway to yourself.

00:36:45.170 --> 00:36:46.810
Slow on this, baby. It's a habit with me.

00:36:47.880 --> 00:36:49.140
Still remember during the war.

00:36:49.820 --> 00:36:51.740
Mind every inch of the way you had to go slow.

00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:53.500
Cut out the war stories, will you?

00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:55.720
How far is it to this Von Reimer estate?

00:36:56.230 --> 00:36:57.450
Max, we're almost there.

00:36:58.860 --> 00:36:59.980
Uh, did you ever see any accident?

00:37:00.400 --> 00:37:02.220
Yeah, I saw a lot of action. I'm a big hero.

00:37:03.240 --> 00:37:05.440
Now, will you get us to this place and stop the talking?

00:37:05.780 --> 00:37:06.960
And I second the motion.

00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:10.340
We ought to be there by now, shouldn't we?

00:37:11.800 --> 00:37:12.240
We're here.

00:38:09.080 --> 00:38:09.800
We have the flashlight.

00:38:46.670 --> 00:38:51.400
Geek. Here, put steady.

00:38:56.310 --> 00:38:58.940
I don't like this. It's like robbing a grave.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.680
This is a special kind of a grave.

00:40:09.250 --> 00:40:09.750
Somebody's coming.

00:40:13.470 --> 00:40:14.870
Help me. Come on. Help me. Come on.

00:40:15.580 --> 00:40:16.580
Cover it up. Cover it up.

00:40:39.020 --> 00:40:39.540
What are you doing?

00:40:40.710 --> 00:40:42.750
We're tourists, Americanish.

00:40:43.130 --> 00:40:46.390
Meine Frau is interested in writings on tombstones.

00:40:46.590 --> 00:40:47.210
It's a hobby.

00:40:47.550 --> 00:40:47.770
Boden.

00:40:48.680 --> 00:40:51.140
Verheimer Estate is open to the public only in the day.

00:40:51.800 --> 00:40:53.380
Sorry, we didn't know.

00:40:53.800 --> 00:40:55.120
Guess we'd better go.

00:40:56.200 --> 00:40:56.700
Good night.

00:41:03.820 --> 00:41:27.340
It's close. Peace.

00:41:27.540 --> 00:41:27.680
Really?

00:41:31.690 --> 00:41:40.320
solid yeah you came up with a little surprise yourself tonight stan with that gun i don't like

00:41:40.320 --> 00:41:48.300
guns how do we get that box worry we'll get it this is just a preview i'm for going in and letting

00:41:48.300 --> 00:41:54.180
those guards have it knock off one of those guys and we never would make the frontier just let me

00:41:54.180 --> 00:41:59.250
handle this we've got plenty of time we've got to have this stuff melted down you got a man to do

00:41:59.250 --> 00:41:59.730
the casting

00:42:01.020 --> 00:42:04.080
A guy named Schmidt has got a little foundry over on the Boomerstrasse.

00:42:04.970 --> 00:42:07.430
Cast gold monkey wrenches for refugees.

00:42:08.620 --> 00:42:09.640
Take a run out there tomorrow.

00:42:26.010 --> 00:42:26.910
Looks good, eh?

00:42:27.520 --> 00:42:28.020
Perfect.

00:42:28.530 --> 00:42:29.550
Solid gold.

00:42:33.420 --> 00:42:36.080
Some of the paint chips off this, what the gold show throw.

00:42:36.300 --> 00:42:38.870
Oh, not paint, lead.

00:42:39.490 --> 00:42:41.050
Makes it look like steel, no?

00:42:42.150 --> 00:42:42.550
How much?

00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:45.060
200 marks.

00:42:45.560 --> 00:42:46.940
No, no, no, I mean for the whole thing.

00:42:47.080 --> 00:42:48.280
200 pounds, maybe more.

00:42:50.120 --> 00:42:51.460
5,000 marks?

00:42:51.580 --> 00:42:52.260
5,000?

00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:53.340
We'll give you 750.

00:42:53.760 --> 00:42:54.240
750?

00:42:54.960 --> 00:42:56.120
Du bist farrikt, impossible.

00:42:56.920 --> 00:42:58.420
750 American dollars.

00:43:02.300 --> 00:43:03.460
800 for no questions.

00:43:05.770 --> 00:43:08.440
When will you bring it?

00:43:09.400 --> 00:43:09.860
A couple of days.

00:43:11.090 --> 00:43:11.650
Thank you very much.

00:43:11.750 --> 00:43:12.170
Oh, no, no, no.

00:43:12.410 --> 00:43:13.310
Not finished yet.

00:43:13.860 --> 00:43:15.540
And now I must age it.

00:43:23.950 --> 00:43:25.730
And now I age it.

00:43:26.620 --> 00:43:27.880
Where did you dig him up?

00:43:29.060 --> 00:43:29.980
No, I go way back.

00:43:31.470 --> 00:43:34.810
Besides casting gold monkey wrenches for refugees, he used to have another racket.

00:43:35.650 --> 00:43:37.530
Casting phony medals for GIs.

00:43:37.810 --> 00:43:40.130
Anything from a Purple Heart to a D.S.C.

00:43:40.780 --> 00:43:42.600
He helped money a guy click with a dime.

00:43:44.380 --> 00:43:48.440
Yeah, he used to turn out a pretty good half-buck piece, too, till they finally put the heat on him.

00:43:49.520 --> 00:43:50.960
You gonna take another crack at that box tonight?

00:43:51.580 --> 00:43:53.000
Oh, I think we better give it a breather.

00:43:53.080 --> 00:43:57.480
If those guards spot us again, they get a little suspicious.

00:43:58.200 --> 00:43:59.820
I still think we ought to barge right it.

00:44:00.510 --> 00:44:03.940
Wait a minute, I've got it. Those guards must have a night off.

00:44:04.280 --> 00:44:05.180
We can find out when.

00:44:05.780 --> 00:44:07.720
Then we go out there and tell the new guards

00:44:07.720 --> 00:44:11.560
that we're a couple of occupation authorities on a security checkup,

00:44:11.740 --> 00:44:14.640
give them some official fast lip, and they give us the run of the place.

00:44:15.020 --> 00:44:16.740
Uh-huh. It'll work.

00:44:17.880 --> 00:44:21.340
Frank, will you step on it? I promise Joanie I'll take her to Bad Nauheim for a swim.

00:44:22.220 --> 00:44:24.380
She'll like it out there. Pretty nice.

00:44:26.220 --> 00:44:28.930
As a matter of fact, I think I'd like to go for a swim myself.

00:44:58.990 --> 00:44:59.250
Bye, Johnny.

00:45:01.760 --> 00:45:04.520
Hi, Stan. I've been looking for you. How'd things go today?

00:45:05.320 --> 00:45:06.640
Oh, fine. Fine.

00:45:10.180 --> 00:45:12.540
You know, after this, I never could go back to the Beehive again.

00:45:16.730 --> 00:45:18.210
There's something wrong, Stan. What is it?

00:45:20.260 --> 00:45:23.200
I don't know. I don't know. I... I... I can't figure Frank.

00:45:24.170 --> 00:45:24.950
What's to figure?

00:45:26.460 --> 00:45:28.140
We could have gotten that box last night easy.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:31.560
Sure, until those men came along.

00:45:32.530 --> 00:45:34.150
Lucky they didn't find out what we were after.

00:45:35.640 --> 00:45:36.780
You've just got to have patience.

00:45:39.450 --> 00:45:40.750
I've got all the patience in the world.

00:45:42.780 --> 00:45:43.760
Then what's bothering you?

00:45:45.750 --> 00:45:46.510
It doesn't add up.

00:45:48.300 --> 00:45:51.270
Frank's the guy that he dives in and he gets things done.

00:45:51.980 --> 00:45:52.480
Remember Chicago?

00:45:53.290 --> 00:45:54.290
Wish I could forget it.

00:45:54.410 --> 00:45:56.110
Well, last night when I wanted to handle those guys,

00:45:56.270 --> 00:45:57.150
suddenly he chickened out.

00:45:58.880 --> 00:45:59.920
I still don't know what you're doing.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:06.390
Well, I'll tell you. I don't think he wanted to get that box last night.

00:46:07.520 --> 00:46:08.500
Why? Why not?

00:46:10.480 --> 00:46:13.060
I'm thinking that he's got an idea that he can get it without us.

00:46:14.860 --> 00:46:15.720
Maybe we'll beat him to it.

00:46:21.890 --> 00:46:23.050
Why is that ever terrific?

00:46:23.380 --> 00:46:24.220
How about a dip, Joanie?

00:46:27.760 --> 00:46:28.200
It's cold.

00:46:28.720 --> 00:46:29.880
Be my guest to a case of...

00:46:30.860 --> 00:46:44.080
it'll be warm as soon as you get in you go on darling i'll sit this out okay fool i need a

00:46:44.080 --> 00:46:52.160
periscope to see us i've got a flash for you a boy's getting ready to throw you a sharp curve

00:46:52.160 --> 00:46:59.100
oh i wondered when he'd get around to that he thinks you might be figuring on the same thing

00:47:00.410 --> 00:47:02.490
Did he say when he plans to pull this?

00:47:03.020 --> 00:47:04.500
You came up before you had a chance to.

00:47:07.160 --> 00:47:07.820
No, by land.

00:47:08.000 --> 00:47:08.800
Too if I see you.

00:47:10.050 --> 00:47:10.970
How did it go at the Foundry?

00:47:15.520 --> 00:47:17.140
That stuff in the box certainly looked real.

00:47:17.400 --> 00:47:17.740
Is it?

00:47:19.110 --> 00:47:20.450
Courtesy of Richard B. Atherton.

00:47:21.600 --> 00:47:23.140
Listen, I've got to go see Keenig.

00:47:23.590 --> 00:47:26.370
Can you take care of Stan for the rest of the day?

00:47:26.950 --> 00:47:27.450
I don't know.

00:47:27.550 --> 00:47:28.990
It was quite a tussle last night.

00:47:29.590 --> 00:47:29.970
He's proud.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:31.780
at the knocking me in the head stage.

00:47:32.970 --> 00:47:35.320
Remember what I told you. Keep sparring.

00:47:35.800 --> 00:47:38.040
He may be bigger, but you've got the speed.

00:47:38.980 --> 00:47:40.960
He's either getting faster or I'm getting slower.

00:47:41.870 --> 00:47:43.650
One of these nights, I may have to hang up my gloves.

00:47:45.810 --> 00:47:47.450
Talk like that. Not even kidding.

00:47:51.980 --> 00:47:52.520
What's going on here?

00:47:52.720 --> 00:47:57.190
A couple of beach athletes kicked sand in her eyes.

00:47:58.020 --> 00:47:58.380
Jerks.

00:48:00.860 --> 00:48:02.420
How's it now? All right.

00:48:03.870 --> 00:48:05.610
Guess your eyes are just too big, dollface.

00:48:06.240 --> 00:48:07.680
Don't he say the sweetest things?

00:48:08.380 --> 00:48:09.920
How about getting dressed and starting back?

00:48:10.460 --> 00:48:11.120
Not yet.

00:48:11.730 --> 00:48:14.430
We've got to find out what night those guys are off.

00:48:14.750 --> 00:48:16.030
I don't want to go now, Stan.

00:48:16.740 --> 00:48:18.420
Gee, I'm just beginning to enjoy it here.

00:48:19.740 --> 00:48:20.980
Can't Frankie go by himself?

00:48:22.980 --> 00:48:24.800
Maybe it'd be better if you went on alone, Frankie.

00:48:25.020 --> 00:48:25.980
Joni and I'll join you later.

00:48:26.470 --> 00:48:28.920
All right. I'll grab the autorail back to Frankfurt.

00:48:30.030 --> 00:48:32.410
I'll meet you tonight, and we'll all have dinner together.

00:48:32.690 --> 00:48:33.790
Why don't you make it after dinner?

00:48:34.240 --> 00:48:35.500
Joni and I'll eat on the way in.

00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:38.140
I'm going to try one of those beer gardens we passed.

00:48:38.810 --> 00:48:41.070
It's so, uh, picturesque.

00:48:41.920 --> 00:48:43.320
Okay, have fun.

00:48:43.850 --> 00:48:45.170
Now, you be sure and wait for us, Frankie.

00:48:45.390 --> 00:48:52.520
This is the life, huh, hon?

00:48:53.540 --> 00:48:55.300
Sure beats car-hopping by a long shot.

00:48:55.700 --> 00:48:58.040
Yeah, no more pounding the hot pavements for my girl.

00:48:59.370 --> 00:48:59.910
Makes me warm.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.730
I'm just thinking about it. I think I'll take that through him now.

00:49:10.950 --> 00:49:11.750
Yeah, Katie.

00:49:12.160 --> 00:49:14.920
Everything depends on it. The success of our whole plan.

00:49:15.620 --> 00:49:16.700
How's about...

00:49:16.700 --> 00:49:18.060
Sure, sure. Help yourself.

00:49:18.660 --> 00:49:20.240
But it's true, as I told you.

00:49:20.670 --> 00:49:22.410
And nothing we can do about it.

00:49:22.940 --> 00:49:26.440
Already the American Air Force has taken over the von Reimer estate.

00:49:27.380 --> 00:49:29.720
And tomorrow, there will be a guard.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:35.900
Oh, the place. You know, alles verboten.

00:49:36.620 --> 00:49:38.760
Must be a way, some way to beat this.

00:49:49.020 --> 00:49:54.360
Remember, the best laid plans of bison men go away sometimes.

00:49:55.770 --> 00:49:59.780
By whom poet Robert Burns, English.

00:50:00.860 --> 00:50:03.860
Oh, yeah, grossartig.

00:50:04.700 --> 00:50:07.730
But there's also some good news, too.

00:50:10.750 --> 00:50:12.410
I have the badge for you.

00:50:14.240 --> 00:50:17.030
See? Deutsche Geheime Criminalpolizei.

00:50:18.120 --> 00:50:19.880
Secret police of Germany.

00:50:21.440 --> 00:50:22.440
Wunderbar, was?

00:50:22.840 --> 00:50:28.160
That will get you in where you are not supposed to be and out to.

00:50:29.040 --> 00:50:29.840
Thanks, Herr Koenig.

00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:35.220
Everything will be fine.

00:50:35.820 --> 00:50:37.460
You will think of something.

00:50:38.680 --> 00:50:39.630
Here. No, thanks.

00:50:41.430 --> 00:50:41.830
Prost!

00:50:51.710 --> 00:50:53.500
It'll be a great night. Great night.

00:50:55.220 --> 00:50:55.780
Sure, great.

00:50:57.020 --> 00:50:59.320
Why are we driving so slow? We'll be late to meet Frank.

00:51:00.030 --> 00:51:01.770
Well, that's, uh, kind of the idea.

00:51:02.970 --> 00:51:05.770
It's gonna be a great night for grave robbing.

00:51:07.090 --> 00:51:07.590
What do you mean?

00:51:08.710 --> 00:51:11.530
Oh, baby, it's all there just waiting for us.

00:51:13.050 --> 00:51:14.390
We'd never help you lift that box.

00:51:14.970 --> 00:51:16.390
Baby, you don't have to lift a finger.

00:51:18.660 --> 00:51:22.900
And another thing, like you said, Frank could have the same idea.

00:51:24.700 --> 00:51:26.760
Maybe I ought to phone him and make sure he's at the hotel.

00:51:33.520 --> 00:51:35.880
Hotel Frederick, Herr Daniel, please, 402.

00:51:39.170 --> 00:51:40.070
It's very important.

00:51:40.350 --> 00:51:43.430
You've got to connect me, please.

00:51:44.760 --> 00:51:46.160
Please, I don't understand.

00:51:46.500 --> 00:51:47.400
Please speak English.

00:51:48.660 --> 00:51:49.700
I think he said Frank, isn't he?

00:51:50.000 --> 00:51:50.380
Yes, Frank.

00:51:51.900 --> 00:51:52.140
Hello.

00:51:52.950 --> 00:51:54.190
I want to speak to Herr Daniel.

00:51:54.400 --> 00:51:55.060
Is he in?

00:51:59.120 --> 00:51:59.860
Okay, thank you.

00:52:02.270 --> 00:52:06.100
Well, he says he doesn't want to be disturbed and orders our orders.

00:52:06.720 --> 00:52:08.040
I guess maybe he's doing a little entertaining.

00:52:08.560 --> 00:52:16.190
At least we know where he is.

00:52:17.210 --> 00:52:18.230
I'm scared to death, Stan.

00:52:19.020 --> 00:52:20.560
Oh, come on, honey. Settle down.

00:52:21.800 --> 00:52:23.120
This is perfect timing, Natalia.

00:52:23.580 --> 00:52:25.020
What if those men out there see us?

00:52:25.320 --> 00:52:26.920
They're sure to find out what we're after.

00:52:28.010 --> 00:52:29.230
I got the answer to that one, too.

00:52:30.440 --> 00:52:31.120
Such a gamble.

00:52:32.450 --> 00:52:36.010
Like you always say, meet long shot stand.

00:53:04.160 --> 00:53:04.360
Shit.

00:53:31.080 --> 00:53:31.460
Thank you.

00:54:07.320 --> 00:54:10.720
There's your hunt, Stan. Nice night for it, isn't it?

00:54:11.060 --> 00:54:11.680
Frank, please.

00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:13.460
Shut up, Julia. Put out that light.

00:54:16.330 --> 00:54:17.690
Right ahead with what you were doing.

00:54:18.970 --> 00:54:23.500
Born digging, me is holding the bag.

00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:34.470
Funny, isn't it? Joni holding the bag.

00:54:38.830 --> 00:54:40.110
Keep on digging the...

00:54:43.750 --> 00:54:44.390
Someone's coming.

00:54:44.710 --> 00:54:45.450
Don't give me that.

00:54:45.950 --> 00:54:46.350
Look!

00:54:50.310 --> 00:54:52.110
Come on, let's get out of here. Back to the car, quick!

00:54:52.950 --> 00:54:53.510
Come on!

00:55:06.040 --> 00:55:25.750
drive i'll get in the back looks like some of them have been turning around in their graves

00:55:35.950 --> 00:55:39.060
Well, what are you waiting for? Why don't you get it over with?

00:55:39.180 --> 00:55:40.580
Don't give me any ideas.

00:55:41.480 --> 00:55:43.180
Look, coming out here tonight was my idea.

00:55:43.380 --> 00:55:45.730
Stan didn't want any part of it. I made him do it.

00:55:45.890 --> 00:55:47.150
Oh, don't be so noble.

00:55:47.490 --> 00:55:48.410
Nobody's being noble.

00:55:50.030 --> 00:55:52.750
And while we're on it, what were you doing out there? Taking the air?

00:55:53.780 --> 00:55:54.980
Just playing a hunch.

00:55:55.280 --> 00:55:56.980
You never had a right hunch in your life.

00:55:58.300 --> 00:55:59.980
Just don't take it out on Stan. He's been on...

00:56:04.240 --> 00:56:05.240
Telling the truth, Stan.

00:56:05.400 --> 00:56:07.300
You heard her.

00:56:07.460 --> 00:56:11.800
Kind of changes the picture.

00:56:12.760 --> 00:56:14.000
Don't blame Joanie, Frank.

00:56:14.100 --> 00:56:14.980
She's a kid that never had a problem.

00:56:15.000 --> 00:56:16.660
You know that better than anybody else.

00:56:16.800 --> 00:56:19.910
She saw that stuff in the box and it threw her.

00:56:21.230 --> 00:56:22.590
You don't have to alibi for me.

00:56:22.920 --> 00:56:24.280
I'm not alibi-ing for you, honey.

00:56:24.340 --> 00:56:27.040
I'm just trying to make Frank see how a thing like that could happen.

00:56:27.820 --> 00:56:29.840
Okay, okay, if that's the way it is, I'll buy it.

00:56:31.148 --> 00:56:33.148
No more funny stuff, understand?

00:56:34.476 --> 00:56:35.256
Okay, Frank.

00:56:36.748 --> 00:56:37.728
Well, I'll forget it if it happened.

00:56:37.872 --> 00:56:38.372
Huh?

00:56:43.116 --> 00:56:45.656
I know something, Joe. You were right. I did have the same idea.

00:56:48.012 --> 00:56:48.852
in the family.

00:56:53.324 --> 00:56:55.084
That's the way it ought to be with a brother and sister.

00:57:05.820 --> 00:57:06.140
Johnny?

00:57:06.684 --> 00:57:07.084
Yes.

00:57:07.516 --> 00:57:08.276
Am I ready to go?

00:57:09.436 --> 00:57:09.696
I'm mad.

00:57:10.364 --> 00:57:11.524
Okay, I'll meet you down the lobby.

00:57:32.620 --> 00:57:36.030
Hey, Frank. Oh, hi, Stan. How do you feel?

00:57:36.370 --> 00:57:39.350
Oh, pretty good. I think I'll be a little better after I get something to eat.

00:57:39.470 --> 00:57:41.980
What about you? Great. Be with you in a minute.

00:57:42.140 --> 00:57:42.380
Okay.

00:57:45.220 --> 00:57:47.320
You tell me that those guards are going to be off on Friday night?

00:57:47.480 --> 00:57:49.500
Yeah, two other guys are replacing him.

00:57:53.070 --> 00:57:53.890
Jody, you about ready?

00:58:06.780 --> 00:58:07.840
and see what I got.

00:58:08.924 --> 00:58:11.924
Take a look at my wallet. I think it's there in the dressing.

00:58:20.764 --> 00:58:24.764
to have him make up some phony official badge, and he had that.

00:58:27.100 --> 00:58:28.560
He's making one up for you, too.

00:58:31.436 --> 00:58:34.656
I don't know if it looks like the McCoy or not, but it'll do to flash on those guards.

00:58:35.756 --> 00:58:37.336
Now, look, when we get out there Friday night,

00:58:37.416 --> 00:58:40.076
we just tell the new guys we're on a security check, see?

00:58:40.556 --> 00:58:43.136
And if they hang around, we just tell them to blow.

00:58:43.396 --> 00:58:43.636
Simple?

00:58:44.844 --> 00:58:45.744
That sounds all right.

00:58:45.984 --> 00:58:46.984
Why, we can...

00:58:47.372 --> 00:58:49.732
Take the stuff out right in front of them if we had to.

00:58:49.964 --> 00:58:51.064
Brother, we're home.

00:58:52.300 --> 00:58:52.920
At my word?

00:58:53.772 --> 00:58:55.172
And if they do give us any trouble,

00:58:55.436 --> 00:58:56.236
We just, uh...

00:58:56.236 --> 00:58:56.876
Let them have it.

00:58:59.244 --> 00:58:59.524
Okay.

00:59:01.244 --> 00:59:03.404
I gotta go. I told Joni I mean it downstairs.

00:59:03.704 --> 00:59:05.124
Now, wait for me. I won't be long.

00:59:20.636 --> 00:59:20.856
Bye-bye.

00:59:21.724 --> 00:59:23.724
Your heart

00:59:24.252 --> 00:59:26.252
My love

00:59:27.068 --> 00:59:29.948
When we're far apart

00:59:30.320 --> 00:59:36.350
My love, don't listen to any one.

00:59:48.260 --> 00:59:55.250
Well, if you can hear her from here, you've got better ears than I have.

00:59:56.380 --> 00:59:59.920
Well, this place hasn't changed a bit. Same smoke, same noise, same beat.

01:00:00.250 --> 01:00:01.030
Only different faces.

01:00:04.010 --> 01:00:05.210
Did I say faces?

01:00:06.920 --> 01:00:08.740
I'm smart, Mom. Let's get out of here.

01:00:09.220 --> 01:00:11.200
Let's not go now. It's so colorful.

01:00:11.910 --> 01:00:12.950
Yeah, it's sigma yellow.

01:00:13.750 --> 01:00:15.210
Wait till she finishes her song.

01:00:31.240 --> 01:00:36.860
And our lives will entwine my love.

01:00:38.030 --> 01:00:39.340
Hey, see you at the door.

01:00:41.090 --> 01:00:41.930
Be right back.

01:00:46.070 --> 01:00:48.930
Don't look now, Frank, that there's a soldier sitting behind us

01:00:48.930 --> 01:00:51.230
that's been staring at you ever since we came in.

01:01:02.270 --> 01:01:02.890
Hey, Jake!

01:01:04.120 --> 01:01:07.200
Well, I'm a son of a gun. Are you still here?

01:01:07.360 --> 01:01:08.660
You know, I thought this joint felt haunted.

01:01:08.860 --> 01:01:09.600
What are you doing in Frankfurt?

01:01:09.900 --> 01:01:11.520
Oh, strictly a tourist this time.

01:01:11.700 --> 01:01:13.760
Still living off the taxpayers, huh?

01:01:13.940 --> 01:01:14.440
What else?

01:01:15.060 --> 01:01:16.540
Come on, I want you to meet the family.

01:01:17.520 --> 01:01:19.160
Family? You didn't take the dive, did you?

01:01:19.280 --> 01:01:20.280
No, no, no.

01:01:21.180 --> 01:01:23.360
Joni, I want you to meet a page out of my past.

01:01:23.500 --> 01:01:25.760
Mike Jankiewicz, my kid sister Joni.

01:01:25.840 --> 01:01:27.140
You remember me telling you about her?

01:01:27.660 --> 01:01:29.980
Well, ten years is a long time ago.

01:01:30.760 --> 01:01:32.000
How are you, Miss, uh...

01:01:32.000 --> 01:01:32.400
Daniel.

01:01:33.890 --> 01:01:35.340
Well, sit down, you big lug.

01:01:36.360 --> 01:01:39.300
Say, uh, you must be pretty handy with the German now, huh?

01:01:39.680 --> 01:01:40.960
Yeah, old but lousy.

01:01:42.840 --> 01:01:45.800
Oh, this is Stan Fabian. Stan, shake hands with Jank.

01:01:46.040 --> 01:01:46.340
Howdy.

01:01:46.440 --> 01:01:46.820
Hi, Stan.

01:01:46.940 --> 01:01:47.360
Sit down, sir.

01:01:48.100 --> 01:01:49.940
Well, tell me, Jank, what are you doing now?

01:01:50.270 --> 01:01:52.750
Well, I've got the Rhine-Main re-enlistment office at headquarters.

01:01:53.460 --> 01:01:54.240
Re-enlistment?

01:01:54.470 --> 01:01:56.890
Oh, leave it to that boy Jank to get a soft touch.

01:01:57.300 --> 01:01:58.900
Well, you look like you're doing all right yourself.

01:01:59.120 --> 01:01:59.960
Taking in Europe is...

01:02:00.420 --> 01:02:04.100
No, strictly as a guest. You see, Stan and Joanie are getting married,

01:02:04.240 --> 01:02:06.280
and I'm a witness. All expenses paid.

01:02:06.710 --> 01:02:08.190
Ham sandwich at the banquet, huh?

01:02:08.960 --> 01:02:09.540
That's right.

01:02:11.070 --> 01:02:13.970
Well, listen, what does that guy do for excitement around here, huh?

01:02:14.130 --> 01:02:15.570
Well, you certainly come to the right party.

01:02:15.970 --> 01:02:18.950
Young man, let me point out a few of the benefits of re-enlisting.

01:02:19.630 --> 01:02:21.150
Strictly as a civilian, bud.

01:02:21.650 --> 01:02:22.630
There goes my commission.

01:02:23.610 --> 01:02:25.110
Well, I better be getting back to the table

01:02:25.110 --> 01:02:27.010
before the Fraulein thinks I'm sticking with the tab.

01:02:27.710 --> 01:02:28.070
See you later?

01:02:28.330 --> 01:02:28.570
Done.

01:02:29.210 --> 01:02:29.970
I knew you were a big...

01:02:30.900 --> 01:02:32.720
Yes, plenty of good old touches to cup, huh?

01:02:32.920 --> 01:02:34.220
Oh, a million of them. See you later?

01:02:34.420 --> 01:02:34.580
Right.

01:02:35.160 --> 01:02:38.340
Oh, what a character, that guy.

01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:41.020
You know, if we'd have had a couple thousand more like him,

01:02:41.140 --> 01:02:42.080
we'd have lost the war.

01:02:42.400 --> 01:02:45.380
Honestly, that guy has more angles for turning a fast buck.

01:02:45.640 --> 01:02:47.260
Uh-huh, fine. Can we go?

01:02:47.500 --> 01:02:47.760
Yeah.

01:03:02.570 --> 01:03:15.420
It is a perfect duplication.

01:03:16.280 --> 01:03:19.160
You will notice I polished the edges to take off the newness.

01:03:22.130 --> 01:03:23.410
Herr Schmidt, you're a real artist.

01:03:23.850 --> 01:03:24.790
Yeah, that looks real all right.

01:03:25.500 --> 01:03:25.820
How much?

01:03:26.380 --> 01:03:28.000
Oh, it is very risky.

01:03:28.340 --> 01:03:29.380
Oh, never mind the build-up.

01:03:29.480 --> 01:03:29.820
How much?

01:03:31.180 --> 01:03:41.940
400 marks okay now these are the tools from the car we bought

01:03:46.020 --> 01:03:51.500
simke eh i will have the molds ready when you get here oh we may bring it late tonight is that

01:03:51.500 --> 01:03:54.590
all right oh at night is better au revoir

01:04:00.920 --> 01:04:03.960
Now, the guards hang out in this tech room in the stable back of the chateau.

01:04:04.100 --> 01:04:06.360
We just walk in, flash our badges,

01:04:06.640 --> 01:04:09.260
and tell them we're investigating a black market operation.

01:04:10.560 --> 01:04:12.020
Suppose they follow us to the cemetery.

01:04:12.590 --> 01:04:13.730
Just tell them to scram.

01:04:15.100 --> 01:04:16.200
And suppose they don't?

01:04:17.000 --> 01:04:19.460
Then I follow your suggestion.

01:04:23.150 --> 01:04:23.770
This fence.

01:04:25.460 --> 01:04:26.260
We on the right road?

01:04:26.980 --> 01:04:27.820
Sure we are.

01:04:29.260 --> 01:04:29.820
Wait a minute.

01:04:34.830 --> 01:04:36.470
This can't be the right road.

01:04:36.630 --> 01:04:37.770
Well, there's only the one road.

01:04:38.650 --> 01:04:39.490
What do you suppose it means?

01:04:40.870 --> 01:04:43.390
Maybe it's just temporary. Sit tight and I'll find out.

01:04:54.090 --> 01:04:56.520
Hey, isn't this the Von Reimer estate?

01:04:56.720 --> 01:04:57.100
Yes, sir.

01:04:57.680 --> 01:04:59.380
This fence is something new, isn't it?

01:04:59.570 --> 01:04:59.970
Yes, sir.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.500
The Air Force has taken the place over as an experimental base.

01:05:03.460 --> 01:05:04.520
When did that happen?

01:05:05.160 --> 01:05:06.000
It's last Wednesday, sir.

01:05:06.740 --> 01:05:10.060
Any chance of, you know, going through the place? We're Americans.

01:05:10.380 --> 01:05:13.820
Sorry, sir, not unless you get a permit signed by the commanding officer in Frankfurt.

01:05:14.380 --> 01:05:15.880
But I doubt if you'll get one, sir.

01:05:21.460 --> 01:05:22.670
Thanks. Thanks very much.

01:05:32.460 --> 01:05:34.060
All right, genius. Got an answer for that one?

01:05:34.560 --> 01:05:36.120
Don't worry. We'll get in there somewhere.

01:05:36.320 --> 01:05:38.140
We can get our brains splattered all over the graveyard.

01:05:38.300 --> 01:05:39.300
A lot of good that's gonna do us.

01:05:58.100 --> 01:05:59.600
Tight squeeze, but I'm not giving up.

01:06:00.220 --> 01:06:07.260
Longshot invested. Long years I've been sweating this thing out.

01:06:07.460 --> 01:06:11.850
I'm going to get that stuff and nothing's going to stop me. Nothing.

01:06:14.560 --> 01:06:16.500
How about Joanie? How's she gonna take this?

01:06:17.350 --> 01:06:21.340
Just don't tell her. We went out there and the same guys were on duty.

01:06:21.480 --> 01:06:22.620
They never changed the guards.

01:06:25.250 --> 01:06:27.880
I'll be there tomorrow and take a look at the layoff.

01:06:29.300 --> 01:06:29.980
I'll come up with some of it.

01:06:30.570 --> 01:06:31.950
I'm sick of your ideas.

01:06:32.210 --> 01:06:36.310
I gotta get my hands on that box.

01:06:37.610 --> 01:06:40.130
Everything depends on everything.

01:06:51.600 --> 01:06:52.620
What's the matter, Stan?

01:06:52.980 --> 01:06:55.430
The way you're acting, you'd think the whole thing was a flop.

01:06:56.470 --> 01:06:58.390
If the car turned off this week, they'll be off next.

01:06:59.430 --> 01:06:59.970
I can't go have you.

01:07:00.320 --> 01:07:05.580
Yeah, I'm just, uh, I'm just a little anxious, honey, that's all.

01:07:06.460 --> 01:07:10.220
It isn't as if we didn't know the gold was there. We saw it.

01:07:13.880 --> 01:07:15.500
What a lovely place for a honeymoon.

01:07:16.450 --> 01:07:24.070
Look, picturesque, bad-gasty.

01:07:25.170 --> 01:07:26.030
What a name.

01:07:26.680 --> 01:07:29.130
Yeah, it's Frank, honey.

01:07:31.630 --> 01:07:31.850
Well?

01:07:32.110 --> 01:07:35.080
Good news, but I'm afraid it's going to take a little time.

01:07:35.600 --> 01:07:38.320
First of all, you couldn't get into that place if you were Eisenhower.

01:07:38.600 --> 01:07:39.080
What do you mean?

01:07:39.820 --> 01:07:42.860
Honey, I didn't want to tell you, but the Air Force has taken over the Von Reimer estate.

01:07:43.000 --> 01:07:45.760
They put a wire fence around that like it was a POW can.

01:07:46.170 --> 01:07:46.810
Oh, no.

01:07:48.400 --> 01:07:52.920
They're putting up a lot of barracks and stuff, but so far, they haven't gotten into the cemetery at all.

01:07:53.100 --> 01:07:54.240
All right, now, what's the good news?

01:07:54.510 --> 01:07:56.250
Well, I got an idea on the way back.

01:07:57.100 --> 01:07:59.840
Remember my friend Jankiewicz, the sergeant we met at Bootsie's?

01:08:00.220 --> 01:08:01.280
You mean you let him in on it?

01:08:01.440 --> 01:08:02.560
Let him in on nothing.

01:08:02.720 --> 01:08:04.820
Remember, he was kidding us about that re-enlistment pitch.

01:08:05.350 --> 01:08:07.270
Well, I found out they're doing some ground experiments

01:08:07.270 --> 01:08:09.350
on Sabre Jet turbines out there.

01:08:09.660 --> 01:08:12.660
Well, I worked on turbines at North American in L.A. last year.

01:08:13.360 --> 01:08:15.740
Jank being in recruiting and with him knowing that, uh,

01:08:15.900 --> 01:08:17.180
I want to stay over here for a while,

01:08:17.320 --> 01:08:19.440
it wouldn't throw him too much if I told him

01:08:19.440 --> 01:08:21.240
I wanted to enlist in the Air Force again.

01:08:22.160 --> 01:08:24.200
You think he could get you assigned to this new base?

01:08:24.930 --> 01:08:28.190
My experience on the Sabre and Jank's drag, I think I'm a cinch.

01:08:29.360 --> 01:08:29.980
How you gonna get the...

01:08:30.400 --> 01:08:34.810
Well, smuggle it out a couple of pieces at a time. Shouldn't take too long.

01:08:35.620 --> 01:08:36.580
Frank, maybe you got something.

01:08:37.900 --> 01:08:39.440
What do you do, Frank? You stay in the army?

01:08:40.060 --> 01:08:42.200
Are you kidding? Once I've liberated the stuff,

01:08:42.320 --> 01:08:44.500
it's over the hill and onto the Riviera.

01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:45.760
That's desertion.

01:08:46.670 --> 01:08:48.670
Terrible. After what happened in Chicago.

01:08:49.740 --> 01:08:50.940
Don't have to worry about Frank.

01:08:52.300 --> 01:08:53.880
Go up and see Jake this afternoon.

01:08:54.320 --> 01:08:55.240
You better go with me, Stan.

01:08:55.400 --> 01:08:57.520
I might need a witness for identification or something.

01:08:57.920 --> 01:08:59.640
Why should we wait till this afternoon? Why don't we go now?

01:09:03.550 --> 01:09:04.950
Isn't this a little beyond the call of duty?

01:09:05.500 --> 01:09:06.860
Don't worry, I've got it all figured out.

01:09:20.930 --> 01:09:22.370
You know, there's sure one for the books, Frank.

01:09:23.060 --> 01:09:25.680
Well, Joanie decided she wanted to go home after the wedding

01:09:25.680 --> 01:09:28.120
and Stan here with the ring in his nose says,

01:09:28.280 --> 01:09:28.580
Okay.

01:09:31.020 --> 01:09:34.580
I figured what's wrong with signing for Hitch and letting Uncle Sam pay the freight.

01:09:34.960 --> 01:09:36.940
They still give guys leave, don't they?

01:09:37.200 --> 01:09:37.720
Why, sure.

01:09:38.350 --> 01:09:41.390
And having connections with the right people, you can always wangle a little extra.

01:09:41.720 --> 01:09:43.440
That's what I figured, Sarge.

01:09:43.770 --> 01:09:44.590
Sign right there, Frank.

01:09:45.990 --> 01:09:48.050
Well, Stan, see you in three years.

01:09:49.170 --> 01:09:52.620
Well, all you gotta do now is take a physical, raise your right hand and you're in.

01:09:58.590 --> 01:09:59.970
Strip down to the waist, I'll be back in...

01:10:01.630 --> 01:10:05.780
I noticed they made an experimental base out of the old Von Reimer estate out there.

01:10:06.000 --> 01:10:07.420
Yeah, just set it up a few days ago.

01:10:07.930 --> 01:10:10.070
You know, Cenk, that'd be pretty good duty out there.

01:10:11.600 --> 01:10:13.870
Oh, I don't claim to be an aeronautical engineer,

01:10:14.070 --> 01:10:16.570
but I do know what makes the little wheels go around,

01:10:16.690 --> 01:10:19.010
and I've had some experience on turbos, too.

01:10:19.860 --> 01:10:22.240
Probably could use a guy like you. Might even get your rating.

01:10:22.920 --> 01:10:24.540
Oh, Doc, I got a live one for you.

01:10:24.760 --> 01:10:25.280
Oh, how you doing?

01:10:26.320 --> 01:10:28.060
Well, Cenk, you got your quarter for the week, I see.

01:10:28.320 --> 01:10:29.980
No trouble at all, sir. He just walked in here.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:50.830
all by himself doesn't look as though there's anything wrong with you have a chair and it brings

01:10:50.830 --> 01:10:55.550
back memories you know if i wasn't getting married oh we've got married men in the service too

01:10:55.550 --> 01:10:59.010
blood pressure normal he doesn't know joanie

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:01.600
She'd wrap her propeller around his skull.

01:11:02.440 --> 01:11:08.220
Take a deep breath. Once again.

01:11:13.800 --> 01:11:14.260
Wrong, Doc?

01:11:17.110 --> 01:11:18.430
Afraid you're not going to make it, young man.

01:11:20.080 --> 01:11:20.460
What do you mean?

01:11:21.050 --> 01:11:23.090
Easy, Doc. As long as he can walk, you know.

01:11:23.980 --> 01:11:25.280
You've got a pronounced heart murmur.

01:11:26.300 --> 01:11:29.240
Doc, I've never had anything wrong with me in my life.

01:11:30.090 --> 01:11:31.850
Have you had a cardiogram taken recently?

01:11:32.980 --> 01:11:35.730
No, but nothing to worry about.

01:11:36.640 --> 01:11:38.420
There's lots of people walking around with heart murmurs.

01:11:39.080 --> 01:11:40.500
But as for getting in the armed services,

01:11:41.230 --> 01:11:42.930
no medical examiner will ever pass you.

01:11:44.680 --> 01:11:45.480
I'm sorry, Mr. Daniel.

01:12:04.640 --> 01:12:08.470
the dough you've got invested. You want to protect it, don't you? About the money I spent,

01:12:08.630 --> 01:12:13.640
forget it. I'm not enlisting. Oh, it's all right if I go ahead and enlist, but with you,

01:12:13.720 --> 01:12:23.980
it's different, huh? I said, forget it. Don't you suggest it in front of Joni. Wait till you see

01:12:23.980 --> 01:12:29.970
what I bought. Some...

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:37.580
I didn't pass the physical.

01:12:39.430 --> 01:12:40.050
Didn't what?

01:12:41.410 --> 01:12:42.770
He's got a bad heart.

01:12:45.840 --> 01:12:47.040
You never told us about it.

01:12:47.180 --> 01:12:48.630
I never knew it myself.

01:12:52.120 --> 01:12:53.360
Looks like the show's over, Joni.

01:12:57.420 --> 01:12:58.020
Can't be.

01:12:58.870 --> 01:12:59.510
Afraid it is.

01:13:04.000 --> 01:13:08.600
But it doesn't have to be. What's the matter with you enlisting?

01:13:10.410 --> 01:13:12.810
Well, why not? Is there something wrong with you, too?

01:13:13.440 --> 01:13:17.480
It wouldn't work out, honey. Even if I signed up, I couldn't get stationed out there.

01:13:17.620 --> 01:13:19.240
I don't know anything about jets or turbines.

01:13:19.540 --> 01:13:22.110
But you were a cook in the army. They still eat, don't they?

01:13:22.170 --> 01:13:22.750
It wouldn't work.

01:13:24.140 --> 01:13:25.680
But you could try Stan, couldn't you?

01:13:25.840 --> 01:13:28.390
Joanie, Stan just doesn't want a witness.

01:13:29.470 --> 01:13:29.970
He doesn't want...

01:13:32.960 --> 01:13:34.780
Don't press me, honey, will you? I've got reasons.

01:13:35.670 --> 01:13:39.140
You've got reasons? What kind of reasons?

01:13:39.300 --> 01:13:40.460
Joanie, there's no sense arguing.

01:13:40.730 --> 01:13:43.730
Oh, yes, there is. He's got reasons not to do it.

01:13:44.350 --> 01:13:46.490
What's the matter with the reason to do it? Me!

01:13:47.280 --> 01:13:51.050
Honey, we'd better call it a day. We've hit too many rocks.

01:13:51.170 --> 01:13:54.970
The whole deal is jinxed. It just isn't supposed to be.

01:13:55.350 --> 01:13:58.090
Oh, it isn't, huh? I told you from the start,

01:13:58.150 --> 01:13:59.970
this was nothing but a goose chase, and I didn't want any...

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:03.140
Any part of it. You're the jinx, Frank.

01:14:03.380 --> 01:14:05.300
You've always been the jinx, and now it's caught up with you.

01:14:05.360 --> 01:14:06.260
Ah, Joni, please.

01:14:06.620 --> 01:14:07.640
You and your honeymoon.

01:14:08.280 --> 01:14:10.140
We were going back on the best tub afloat.

01:14:10.540 --> 01:14:11.800
Well, I've got plans now.

01:14:12.030 --> 01:14:14.270
And all I want from you is my ticket back home.

01:14:14.630 --> 01:14:15.710
And I'm sailing alone.

01:14:17.910 --> 01:14:19.520
Joni! Joni!

01:14:22.320 --> 01:14:23.380
Joni, I want to talk to you.

01:14:23.440 --> 01:14:24.320
I don't want to talk to you.

01:14:25.000 --> 01:14:26.980
Just give me my ticket. I want to go home.

01:14:29.240 --> 01:14:29.980
Honey, you'll get home on...

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:33.440
Things are gonna be all right, and you'll have your security, I promise you.

01:14:33.500 --> 01:14:35.480
You promise? You promise what?

01:14:35.910 --> 01:14:38.950
A life in that hash house? Jumping in auto horns?

01:14:39.200 --> 01:14:41.080
Hearing you say everything's gonna be all right, baby?

01:14:41.730 --> 01:14:43.610
What about my honeymoon? What about my security?

01:14:43.910 --> 01:14:47.180
Shut up, Joanie! No matter how you talk, I'm not gonna enlist.

01:14:48.350 --> 01:14:50.390
Honey, you know that I'm nuts about you. I'd do anything for you.

01:14:50.470 --> 01:14:51.790
Anything in the world. You know that.

01:14:52.100 --> 01:14:53.640
If you really loved me...

01:14:53.860 --> 01:14:54.620
Why, Joanie...

01:14:54.620 --> 01:14:57.090
Don't touch me. I thought you had class.

01:14:57.990 --> 01:14:59.130
Why, you're nothing!

01:15:03.320 --> 01:15:06.130
You're wrong. You're wrong, baby.

01:15:07.210 --> 01:15:10.190
I'm something. I'm gonna tell you something.

01:15:11.340 --> 01:15:14.690
Nobody knows this. When I was in that army, I killed a couple of guys.

01:15:14.790 --> 01:15:17.540
One of them was an MP officer. That's why I can't enlist.

01:15:17.660 --> 01:15:18.880
If I go back in, that'll have it for good.

01:15:20.480 --> 01:15:22.600
Waited 10 years to hear you say that, Stan.

01:15:23.620 --> 01:15:24.600
And long years.

01:15:26.040 --> 01:15:27.820
All right, Herr Koenig, you can take him now.

01:15:31.500 --> 01:15:34.400
Confession is good for the soul, Herr Fabian, eh?

01:15:35.300 --> 01:15:36.720
Deutsche Kommunalpolizei!

01:15:37.140 --> 01:15:39.640
You are under arrest for the murder of Lieutenant Atherton.

01:15:39.800 --> 01:15:50.290
If something would have enlisted, it would have touched you.

01:15:52.050 --> 01:15:52.450
Upfield.

01:16:06.140 --> 01:16:07.530
I guess I had it coming.

01:16:15.680 --> 01:16:17.260
This is a beautiful tray, Mr. Atherton.

01:16:17.510 --> 01:16:18.770
Looks like steel, no?

01:16:19.380 --> 01:16:19.800
Solid.

01:16:20.100 --> 01:16:20.260
Cool.

01:16:21.100 --> 01:16:24.000
It's a souvenir wedding present to both of you.

01:16:24.980 --> 01:16:26.520
Ah, Joanie's my wedding present.

01:16:28.370 --> 01:16:29.370
Isn't she beautiful?

01:16:30.220 --> 01:16:33.820
Like the lady of the lake.

01:16:34.000 --> 01:16:35.810
By the writer Walter Scott.

01:16:36.270 --> 01:16:36.730
English.

01:16:37.290 --> 01:16:38.010
Scotch.

01:16:38.450 --> 01:16:38.990
Scotch.

01:16:39.330 --> 01:16:40.070
Wunderbar.

01:16:42.030 --> 01:16:44.980
To the bright and to the grove.

01:16:46.880 --> 01:16:47.440
They shall live.
